# Ubuntu Automation Project Rules

## Testing and Development Guidelines

- **Never test scripts locally** - Installation scripts are designed to run on Ubuntu servers and will not work in local development environments
- **Never create fix scripts** - When installation scripts have issues, fix the source scripts directly rather than creating temporary fix scripts
- **Focus on source script fixes** - Users will rerun corrected installation scripts rather than attempting to fix existing installations
- **No local execution** - Do not attempt to run installation commands or scripts in the development environment

## Code Standards

- Always use proper bash scripting practices with error handling
- Maintain consistent logging to `/srv/apps/logs/`
- Use shared functions from `utils/shared_functions.sh`
- Follow existing patterns for email configuration and systemd service management 